  "text": "2:41¢ all ¥ @\n< 12 rules for life 0\n1 of 12 ideas collected\n2a the lobster principle\nyour posture sends a loud signal to\nyour brain. if you slump, you tell your\ninternal systems that you are at the\nbottom of the pile. your body reacts\nby dropping chemicals that regulate\nmood. you feel weaker, so you shrink\nmore. it is a biological spiral into\nchaos.\nyou snap the loop by taking up space.\nstanding tall exposes your chest and\nthroat to the world. this voluntary risk\nforces your mind to switch from fear\nto focus. the world treats you like a\nvictor only when you look like one.\n& a\n",
